--- import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro"; import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro"; import "../../styles/standards-poster.css"; import "../../styles/extended.css"; import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj25.json"; --- <StandardPageLayout code={metadata.code} standardType={metadata.framework} title={metadata.title} description={metadata.description} issued={metadata.issued} latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment} status={metadata.status} summary={metadata.summary} bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice} > <Fragment slot="toc"> <PageToc items={[{"id":"s1","label":"Conceptual Framework Linkage"},{"id":"s2","label":"Scope — Consolidated Financial Statements Only"},{"id":"s3","label":"Comprehensive Income Defined — Net Profit Plus Other Comprehensive Income"},{"id":"s4","label":"Components of Other Comprehensive Income"},{"id":"s5","label":"Presentation Format — Single Statement or Two Consecutive Statements"},{"id":"s6","label":"A RECURRING J-GAAP THEME — Individual Statements Have No Comprehensive Income Figure"},{"id":"s7","label":"Recycling — Reclassification to Profit or Loss"},{"id":"s8","label":"Worked Example — Calculating Total Comprehensive Income"},{"id":"s9","label":"Worked Example — Comparing Consolidated and Individual Presentation"},{"id":"s10","label":"Disclosure Requirements"},{"id":"s11","label":"Critical Judgments"},{"id":"s12","label":"Relationship to IAS/IFRS"},{"id":"s13","label":"Statement Mapping"},{"id":"s14","label":"Related Standards"},{"id":"s15","label":"Glossary"}]} /> </Fragment> <div class="wrap"> <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Introducing a genuinely new concept to Japanese financial reporting</div><div class="principle">BEFORE ASBJ Statement No. 25, J-GAAP had NO "comprehensive income" concept AT ALL — unrealised gains/losses on securities, foreign currency translation adjustments, and similar items simply moved DIRECTLY within the Net Assets section's Valuation and Translation Adjustments component, WITHOUT ever being COMBINED with net profit into a SINGLE, presented total. This Statement introduced "COMPREHENSIVE INCOME" (包括利益) as a GENUINE new presentation concept — REQUIRING a combined figure showing net profit PLUS all "OTHER COMPREHENSIVE INCOME" movements for the period.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Consolidated Financial Statements Only</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A requirement that applies only at the group reporting level</div><div class="principle">This Statement applies ONLY to CONSOLIDATED financial statements — companies preparing consolidated statements must present COMPREHENSIVE INCOME; companies' OWN INDIVIDUAL (non-consolidated) financial statements are NOT required to present a comprehensive income figure or statement (Section 6).</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Comprehensive Income Defined — Net Profit Plus Other Comprehensive Income</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A single combined figure capturing the full period movement</div><div class="text-supporting">COMPREHENSIVE INCOME = NET PROFIT (or loss) for the period PLUS "OTHER COMPREHENSIVE INCOME" (その他の包括利益, OCI) — the period's movement in items that PREVIOUSLY moved DIRECTLY within Net Assets' Valuation and Translation Adjustments component WITHOUT passing through a comprehensive income TOTAL. Together, these give a FULLER picture of the TOTAL change in a shareholder's economic position DURING the period, beyond just the traditional "bottom line" net profit figure.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Components of Other Comprehensive Income</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">The same underlying items previously tracked only within Net Assets</div><div class="th cols-13-17"><span>OCI component</span><span>Source</span></div> <div class="tr cols-13-17"><span>Unrealised gains/losses on Available-for-Sale securities</span><span>ASBJ Statement No. 10 (Financial Instruments)</span></div> <div class="tr cols-13-17"><span>Deferred hedge gains/losses</span><span>ASBJ Statement No. 10 (Financial Instruments)</span></div> <div class="tr cols-13-17"><span>Foreign currency translation adjustments</span><span>Consolidation of foreign subsidiaries</span></div> <div class="tr cols-13-17"><span>Remeasurements of Defined Benefit Plans</span><span>ASBJ Statement No. 19 / No. 26 (Retirement Benefits)</span></div> <div class="tr cols-13-17"><span>Share of OCI of equity-method affiliates</span><span>ASBJ Statement No. 16 (Equity Method)</span> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Presentation Format — Single Statement or Two Consecutive Statements</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Two acceptable formats, broadly mirroring IAS 1</div><div class="text-supporting">A company may present comprehensive income EITHER as a SINGLE, CONTINUOUS statement (starting with revenue, working down to net profit, then ADDING other comprehensive income items to arrive at TOTAL comprehensive income) OR as TWO SEPARATE but CONSECUTIVE statements (a Statement of Income arriving at net profit, IMMEDIATELY followed by a separate Statement of Comprehensive Income starting from that net profit figure) — broadly MIRRORING IAS 1's OWN single-statement/two-statement presentation choice internationally.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>A RECURRING J-GAAP THEME — Individual Statements Have No Comprehensive Income Figure</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The same consolidated/individual dual-track pattern seen elsewhere in J-GAAP</div><div class="text-supporting">This Statement's LIMITATION to CONSOLIDATED financial statements ONLY is a RECURRING structural theme seen ELSEWHERE in J-GAAP — most notably in retirement benefit accounting (see the companion ASBJ Statement No. 19 poster, where CONSOLIDATED statements recognise actuarial remeasurements IMMEDIATELY while INDIVIDUAL statements continue GRADUAL amortisation). An entity's OWN individual (non-consolidated) financial statements CONTINUE to present Net Assets movements WITHOUT a combined comprehensive income TOTAL — illustrating a genuinely DISTINCTIVE, recurring J-GAAP PATTERN of applying MORE internationally-aligned treatment at the CONSOLIDATED level while RETAINING more traditional, less internationally-aligned treatment at the INDIVIDUAL statement level.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Recycling — Reclassification to Profit or Loss</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Most OCI components are eventually reclassified through profit or loss</div><div class="text-supporting">MOST other comprehensive income components are SUBSEQUENTLY "RECYCLED" (reclassified) to the Statement of Income upon a TRIGGERING event — for example, unrealised gains on Available-for-Sale securities are recycled upon SALE of the security, and foreign currency translation adjustments are recycled upon DISPOSAL of the foreign subsidiary — ensuring these amounts EVENTUALLY flow through profit or loss, just at a DIFFERENT (later) point in time than immediate recognition would have.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Calculating Total Comprehensive Income</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Combining net profit with the period's OCI movements</div> <div class="worked"><div class="wk-title">Example: A consolidated group's comprehensive income for the year</div><div class="wk-body">A consolidated group reports net profit of ¥1,200,000,000 for the year. During the same year, it recognises ¥80,000,000 of unrealised gains on Available-for-Sale securities and a ¥30,000,000 foreign currency translation LOSS.</div><div class="wk-answer">TOTAL COMPREHENSIVE INCOME = ¥1,200,000,000 (net profit) + ¥80,000,000 (unrealised securities gain) − ¥30,000,000 (translation loss) = <strong>¥1,250,000,000</strong> — presented EITHER within a single continuous statement or as a SEPARATE statement immediately following the Statement of Income.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Comparing Consolidated and Individual Presentation</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The same OCI movements, presented differently by statement type</div> <div class="worked"><div class="wk-title">Example: The same unrealised gain, consolidated vs individual statements</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, the ¥80,000,000 unrealised securities gain also appears in the PARENT company's OWN individual (non-consolidated) financial statements.</div><div class="wk-answer">In the CONSOLIDATED financial statements, this ¥80,000,000 is presented WITHIN a comprehensive income TOTAL, as REQUIRED by this Statement. In the parent's OWN INDIVIDUAL financial statements, the SAME ¥80,000,000 movement is recognised WITHIN Net Assets (Valuation and Translation Adjustments) as BEFORE, but <strong>NO comprehensive income figure or statement is presented</strong> — this Statement's requirement simply does NOT extend to individual, non-consolidated reporting.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 25 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Total comprehensive income and its allocation between owners of the parent and non-controlling interests</span><span>Each component of other comprehensive income, and related tax effects</span><span>Reclassification adjustments recycled to profit or loss during the period</span></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div> <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether to present a single continuous statement or two consecutive statements</span></div></div> <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally minimal — this Statement is primarily a presentational standard reflecting amounts already determined elsewhere</span></div></div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IAS 1</div><div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span>J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 25)</span><span>IFRS (IAS 1)</span></div> <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Presentation format choice</span><span>Single statement or two consecutive statements</span><span>Single statement or two consecutive statements — converged</span></div> <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Applies to individual/separate financial statements</span><span>NO — consolidated only</span><span>YES — IAS 1 applies at whatever level financial statements are prepared</span> <div class="note">The comprehensive income CONCEPT and presentation CHOICES are genuinely CONVERGED with IAS 1 — the notable divergence is J-GAAP's LIMITATION of the requirement to CONSOLIDATED statements only, part of the BROADER recurring consolidated/individual dual-track pattern in J-GAAP.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every comprehensive income event lands</div><div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div> <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Other comprehensive income movement</span><span><span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> Comprehensive income statement</span><span>Consolidated statements only</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div><div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div> <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 5</span><span>Supplies the Valuation and Translation Adjustments Net Assets component OCI items are drawn from</span></div> <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 19</span><span>Retirement Benefits (Part 3) — supplies the Remeasurements of Defined Benefit Plans OCI component</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cn span2"> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Comprehensive income (包括利益)</div><div class="glossary-def">Net profit plus other comprehensive income for the period, presented only in consolidated financial statements.</div></div> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Other comprehensive income (その他の包括利益)</div><div class="glossary-def">Items of income and expense not recognised in profit or loss, such as unrealised securities gains/losses, deferred hedges, translation adjustments, and defined benefit plan remeasurements.</div></div> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Reclassification adjustment (recycling)</div><div class="glossary-def">The subsequent transfer of a previously recognised OCI item into profit or loss upon a triggering event, such as sale of a security.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</span></div></div> </div> </StandardPageLayout> 